[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560454144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3560454144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3560454144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UODgA","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T22:45:54Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T22:45:54Z","body":"this looks like an incredible improvement! looking at the video, i do have one question though: why do some items in the tree become blue temporarily? is that a remnant of the old method that didn’t take x pos into account? if so, it should probably go, as the hierarchy like this pr consistently adds is a much clearer indication of the result of the drag and drop.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560454144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560459126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3560459126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3560459126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UOEt2","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T22:47:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T22:53:28Z","body":"Blue means pushed to inspector! I realised while working on this, and it's an indicator that's unrelated to this PR. Hovering on something for a bit turns it blue and shows it in the inspector, so that you can then drag the node into the blue node's export slots, if any.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560459126/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560652532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3560652532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3560652532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UOz70","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T23:37:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T23:37:22Z","body":"Looks very promising!\r\n(I haven't checked the code)\r\n\r\nBut note that drag dropping is not for nodes only (or rather just for the tree items, which in case of the scene tree represent nodes). E.g. you can drag resources onto the nodes, in such case the new indicators are wrong:\r\n\r\nv4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]|v4.6.dev.gh-112993 [c599891c2]\r\n-|-\r\n![Godot_v4 5 1-stable_win64_H0DRNXFC0H](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a77aaa2b-95b7-4991-abeb-c8d853c3b68e)|![godot windows editor x86_64_t9D0EKJjqV](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c925a57-b923-4778-ae30-bf8513997c1d)\r\n\r\nAlso be sure to take in mind potential user-usages of the Tree node.\r\nCurrently (without this PR) visual drop indicators are hard coded to be shown when `Tree.drop_mode_flags != DROP_MODE_DISABLED`, I think we could potentially change this to be somehow configurable (with default config preserving the previous behavior?). Given how the new indicators are much more complex visually it makes sense to have some control over them. However the indicators will be fixed for dropping resources onto nodes etc., probably the same level of customization should be available for the users.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560652532/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560854393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3560854393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3560854393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UPlN5","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T00:58:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T01:13:23Z","body":"@kleonc Makes sense, I'll start moving in that direction. Thank you for having a look.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3560854393/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583963387","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3583963387","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3583963387,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VnvD7","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T02:23:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T02:23:32Z","body":"With the addition of a pair of if statements, in the specific case that `DROP_MODE_ON_ITEM` is the only enabled flag for a drag:\r\n  - The dropdown arrow and stub are replaced with the prior rectangular selection, but now styled with the editor's accent color, much like the border that appears on a compatible inspector property slot, or as noted above, the \"blue\" that the text of the target node adopts when pushed to the inspector. This is registered in the theme as `Tree > drop_on_item_color`.\r\n- Indent space is no longer considered for choosing this drop target.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"361\" height=\"140\" alt=\"(_) tree_test tscn - Unnamed Project - Godot Engine Thu, 27 Nov 05_54_55\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/091a242c-2ab3-42bf-8f7f-06aa720cf409\" />\r\n\r\nThrough this, the visualization of a \"child\" in this specific case is no more, replaced with something more analogous to the resulting action - an image replacing the `Texture` slot of a Sprite2D, a script replacing the `Script` slot of any node.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583963387/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3935560582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-3935560582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":3935560582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qk-OG","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T15:20:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T15:20:46Z","body":"Thank you for the feedback. Not only should what you mentioned be addressed, but it also looks like the drop line is too thin compared to the relationship line in hiDPI.\r\n\r\nI turned this into a draft once I was made aware how much of the engine interface relied on Tree, for very different purposes. I've been meaning to do a proper survey to ensure I don't mess with any of the visual metaphors for the many ways it's used. Additionally, I've identified an improvement to be made in the input editor tree that I'd like to PR first, before this one.\r\n\r\nWill resume work on this soon.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3935560582/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4064013147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4064013147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4064013147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yO-tb","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-15T22:13:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-15T22:21:09Z","body":"Introduced validation against dropping onto self or descendants.\r\n\r\nIn the current master, attempting a drop into self shows the current drop indicator, and attempting one that would make a parent into its own grandchild also results in SceneTreeDock's `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG` \"Selection changed at some point. Can't reparent.\"\r\n\r\nNow, it doesn't show drop indicators, changes the cursor to reinforce this as well, and catches it internally. The push to inspector when hovering still works fine.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/22b225d3-7b6b-4c74-a482-f31be0e5a52c\r\n\r\nStill investigating hiDPI, but it should be a minor fix. The additional flag proposal for Input Map would be better suited as a follow up. I'd like reviews to continue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4064013147/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066702307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4066702307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4066702307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yZPPj","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T10:35:56Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T10:35:56Z","body":"Getting there! Perhaps this specific situation is a bit awkward: when dragging a node that is already the first and / or last child of its parent onto its parent again, the line appears above or below it even though it won't move. \r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1fbfc2d4-99f1-4f5e-91e6-d8f0d86b52ca\r\n\r\nThis might be desired for consistency, and perhaps the suggestion that follows is too nitpicky, but… it might work more intuitively if the line simply goes to the node where it's placed already in those specific cases?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066702307/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4070565477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4070565477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4070565477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yn-Zl","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T21:00:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T03:25:45Z","body":"Update!\r\n\r\n- Now the line has a pixel perfect overlap, on every display scale.\r\n- The drop indicator's been moved to its own `CanvasItem`, so it can display over the selection box, which reappeared as a problem.\r\n- The scope of the \"invalid\" cursor icon is reduced, so that it doesn't show up when hovering over self, only when hovering over children.\r\n- @AdriaandeJongh's recommendation has been implemented, for case A - when the parent is the same. Doing so was fairly nontrivial, but greatly improves feel. It's worth noting that this isn't worth extending to case B, since case C isn't possible. I also think it's good to reinforce the change of parent anyway.\r\n\r\n| Case A | Case B | Case C |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| <img width=\"266\" height=\"190\" alt=\"tree-case-a\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8cee0ac3-5e73-4046-90c2-688c7231e2f7\" /> | <img width=\"266\" height=\"190\" alt=\"tree-case-b\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d7651ca-ed85-4009-9b23-31308d80bb35\" /> | <img width=\"266\" height=\"190\" alt=\"tree-case-c\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3735d541-3e36-42df-803f-e34e8e554997\" /> |\r\n\r\nI will continue to tinker and find places to reduce bloat.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4070565477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4082304554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4082304554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4082304554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zUwYq","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T12:55:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T12:55:44Z","body":"The invalid reparent indicator still shows when multiple nodes are selected:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e58e79e7-aeee-44a6-b171-2633b6cc6161\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4082304554/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4084077879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4084077879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4084077879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zbhU3","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T16:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T17:41:06Z","body":"Thank you for the approvals.\r\n\r\nI was aware of the problem with multiple nodes, but due to the present solution's reliance on `selected_item`, it's best saved for a follow up or would add a lot more complexity, especially for an edge case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4084077879/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4084494259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4084494259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4084494259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zdG-z","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T17:53:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T19:24:49Z","body":"> Note that you can't drag-and-drop the last item of a tree outside its parent by moving it at the bottom (after the end of the tree). You have to make it a child of the root node all the way to the top instead.\r\n\r\nTry dragging to the left. 😊\r\nOr do you mean you would prefer everything past the end of the tree to be treated as free space for the root node? Looking into this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4084494259/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4103068435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4103068435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4103068435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70j9sT","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-21T10:52:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T21:30:32Z","body":"After investigating @Calinou's recommendation, I stumbled into certain design conflicts, solving which require generalisations that aren't currently safe to make, and better saved for a follow-up.\r\n\r\nDragging into free space, for:\r\n| Scene Tree | FileSystem | Input Map |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| <img width=\"286\" height=\"314\" alt=\"(_) animation_tree tscn - test - Godot Engine Sat, 21 Mar 14_46_31\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbfa9964-8c8a-4687-94eb-1f88c73ad92e\" /> | <img width=\"284\" height=\"318\" alt=\"(_) animation_tree tscn - test - Godot Engine Sat, 21 Mar 14_46_43\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/940fefe4-cbf1-494f-ba18-684cdecb1300\" /> | <img width=\"233\" height=\"322\" alt=\"animation_tree tscn - test - Godot Engine Sat, 21 Mar 14_52_11\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73290fc5-9611-462e-a2e6-7ebd3f8bb599\" /> |\r\n| As last child of visible root | As last child of last child (res://) of hidden root | As last child of hidden root\r\n| Can be default behaviour | Needs flag specific to Tree instance announcing this intent | Default, then further resolved by [#14338](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14338) |\r\n\r\nWhile all three ingest drops with their own implementations, as is the user expected to, what the \"root\" effectively is for each of these varies. With `hide_root` being a stylistic choice, not a functional one (as evidenced by Input Map), it is unsuitable to use in interpreting this. There needs to be another variable, something like `min_drop_depth`, that can announce 0 (root level) as SceneTreeDock and Input Map's choice, and 1 (res:// & Favorites level) as FileSystemDock's. Or more simply, it could just be `ignore_root`.\r\n\r\nWhile the code for this is largely ready, as well as `keep_depth` (needed for [#14338](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14338)), adding them now would necessitate another round of testing, which after the approvals already I'm not sure is the best idea. The addition of these would also be grounds for simplifying the ingestion code that SceneTreeDock and Input Map use for their drops.\r\n\r\nSo, in the meantime, what could been added painlessly is: a new TreeItem flag called `drop_mode_on_item_allowed`, which controls its ability to accept children, so now files in the FileSystemDock do not have the reparent indicator that folders do.\r\n\r\n~~If all that's okay, then this is ready. The rest will follow, in time for 4.7.~~\r\n\r\n---\r\nIt has only just occurred to me that I can disable `drop_mode_on_item_allowed` on FileSystemDock's root... please wait.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4103068435/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4107068428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4107068428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4107068428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70zOQM","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-22T22:00:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T22:45:41Z","body":"Summarising my thoughts from earlier.\r\n\r\nThe addition of a new `accepts_children` flag for TreeItems allows us to exclude them from an adoptive hover. So the reparent indicator no longer appears over files in FileSystemDock, and its null root is now completely inaccessible.\r\n\r\n| Impossible child | Untouchable root |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- |\r\n|<img width=\"544\" height=\"161\" alt=\"(_) Player tscn - openseam - Godot Engine Mon, 23 Mar 02_41_24\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e7d6efc-e69b-4c0a-ab8a-67b1dc7fb98d\" />|<img width=\"546\" height=\"186\" alt=\"(_) Player tscn - openseam - Godot Engine Mon, 23 Mar 02_39_38\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31a4788a-f287-46c1-ab8a-ac7e87d77f38\" />|\r\n\r\nThis also lays the groundwork for...\r\n\r\n1.  @Calinou's recommendation, which entails that whenever a Tree is updated, the eldest and lowermost node with `accepts_children` is nominated as the \"fallback root,\" and accepts anything dropped in the free space below as last child. A draft for this is ready, but will take time. This would also be a good place to refactor parts of the editor's individual Tree instances, as they will get pulled in regardless.\r\n\r\n2. Implementing [#14338](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14338) as a `drop_lock_depth` flag for Input Map Editor, so that drags are able to maintain their hierarchy: actions only rearrange among actions, mappings only ever attempt to switch parents, and nothing invalid is attempted. This needs the prior feature to be rock solid first, so that this case isn't prematurely excluded from testing.\r\n\r\n3. @KoBeWi's recommendation of better handling multi-select drags, which should then adhere to all the new rules.\r\n\r\nThese are best saved for successive PR's.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4107068428/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4108132825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4108132825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":4108132825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc703SHZ","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T05:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T05:36:32Z","body":"Sounds good to me!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4108132825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136264534","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112993#issuecomment-4136264534","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112993","id":413626